{"title":"2023 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/8/178ef0c25cb393195368ae91e70341404562e677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1, \\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d3818b42481a171d953bd6790c068d34809df183.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> respectively, they are externally tangent to each other. The diameters of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c855dc7ee38b4b39105dbab0b113def7ea90a1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB,CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> respectively, satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89ee5420004c3b2a8f1f0cf81594b54dbbb1da5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\parallel CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is an external tangent of the circles. The third circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238ebc976ecd51f0687763bc3e5de75a0c543896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> and is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. The minimum possible value of the radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d0f5d72741e1b57a8ac058d675f1621a5798bb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+b\\sqrt{c}}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"39\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is a squarefree positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a643bcc8195884f4fc1e16966f6f3d6ad6fe2c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e947add5766b9f26f6dfe73d9425d87664416459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/d/dcd508cdc6e767a546581d0d9af73ec27ea86708.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200);  pair B = (0,0); pair A = (0,2); pair D = (4,0); pair C = (4,8);  dot(A);  dot(B);  dot(C); dot(D);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, NE); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, SE);  draw(A--B, dashed); draw(C--D, dashed); draw(B--D, black+linewidth(1));  pair O1 = (0,1); pair O2 = (4,4); pair O3 = ((4*sqrt(13)-4)/3,(65-8*sqrt(13))/9);  draw(circle(O1,1), black); draw(circle(O2,4), black); draw(circle(O3,(65-8*sqrt(13))/9), blue+linewidth(1.2));  label(&quot;$\\omega_1$&quot;, (-1,1), NW); label(&quot;$\\omega_2$&quot;, (6.5,7), NE); label(&quot;$\\omega_3$&quot;, (0.5,7), N); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"315\" /> </center><p> We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/511c2867353cb84e7be131a145a0e3dfcac8068c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BD = \\sqrt{(4+1)^2-(4-1)^2} = 4.\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"32\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e06691c1d984a2e6481518e9478a878ba71f84d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/131c888579b35136842c6ade87a7f8c62cb23824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = (4,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5eef0d67bdd68c8545ddc871ba6913e3e0a1fa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (0,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/926be1a06061d12e8b11c06288cdb7938118176f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (4,8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />. Suppose the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, the radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238ebc976ecd51f0687763bc3e5de75a0c543896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/876f0b1a551d23f5530ad2118c966e099051abc1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a^2+(b-2)^2=(a-4)^2+(b-8)^2=b^2.\\]\" width=\"318\" height=\"20\" /> From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/2629a74b7a84fc17e6afe44d7726c88e972492e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2+(b-2)62=(a-4)^2+(b-8)^2\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"20\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31ef9b590b88c9ba34d6eb3f90fcf76b11353a0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8a+12b=76\\implies a=\\frac{19}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}b.\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"37\" /> Substituting into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4b2a846fcb7cc9cfd9d01920dd598fec826075.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2+(b-2)^2=b^2\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/8/19871a9bedc90f779ea1cde94a38f3b4f2a0659f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{9}{4}b^2-\\frac{65}{2}b+\\frac{377}{4}\\implies b = \\frac{65-8\\sqrt{13}}{9}\\implies 65-8+13+9=\\boxed{79}.\\]\" width=\"528\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018024300\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 137/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6746/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31910:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018024300 and revision id 274638. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}